    "created_at": "2025-08-21T00:35:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-21T00:35:15Z",
    "body": "On the general principle of making custom elements as capable as built-ins, I am in support of this.\n\nHowever, it is worth questioning whether this particular capability is actually a useful one. `<progress>` and `<meter>` are not the most-used elements ever, so I wonder how many web developers know about, or benefit from, this ability. If we were designing those elements today, would we judge the distinction important enough to split them and create a new labelable-but-not-form-associated category? Or would we instead just leave them un-labelable, or make them form-associated?",
